            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 74-year-old female, admitted on 27/02/2014 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. Her condition improved satisfactorily and she was discharged in stable condition. Please arrange follow-up including spirometry and review of maintenance inhalation therapy at your earliest convenience. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
